{% extends "tool_layout" %}
{% import "icons" as icons %}

{# js/tools/pages/hash-generator.mjs builds the algorithm list and results.
   On a variant's page (e.g. SHA-256 Hash Generator), its algorithm comes
   first. #}

{% block tool %}
<section class="panel panel-pad tool-panel" id="hash-tool" data-first="{{ variant.from if variant else '' }}"
    aria-label="Hash generator">
    <div class="seg hash-mode" role="radiogroup" aria-label="What to hash">
        <input type="radio" class="btn-check" name="hash-mode" id="mode-text" value="text" checked>
        <label class="seg-btn" for="mode-text">Text</label>
        <input type="radio" class="btn-check" name="hash-mode" id="mode-file" value="file">
        <label class="seg-btn gap-2" for="mode-file">{{ icons.icon("file") }} File</label>
    </div>

    <div id="hash-text-box" class="mt-3">
        <label for="hash-text" class="visually-hidden">Text to hash</label>
        <textarea id="hash-text" class="form-control tool-area" rows="5" spellcheck="false"
            placeholder="Type or paste text. It's hashed as UTF-8."></textarea>
    </div>
    <div id="hash-file-box" class="mt-3" hidden>
        <input type="file" id="hash-file" class="visually-hidden">
        <label for="hash-file" class="hash-drop" id="hash-drop">
            {{ icons.icon("file") }}
            <span id="hash-file-name">Choose a file, or drop it here</span>
            <span id="hash-file-size" class="small text-secondary">Any size: it's read in pieces and never uploaded.</span>
        </label>
        <div class="progress mt-2" id="hash-progress" role="progressbar" aria-label="Hashing" aria-valuemin="0"
            aria-valuemax="100" hidden>
            <div class="progress-bar"></div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <fieldset class="mt-3">
        <legend class="small text-secondary mb-1">Algorithms</legend>
        <div id="hash-algorithms" class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-3"></div>
    </fieldset>
    <div class="row g-2 mt-2">
        <div class="col-md">
            <label for="hash-key" class="small text-secondary">HMAC key (optional)</label>
            <input id="hash-key" class="form-control font-monospace" type="text" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off"
                placeholder="Leave empty for plain hashes" data-1p-ignore data-lpignore="true" data-bwignore="true"
                data-form-type="other">
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-auto">
            <label for="hash-format" class="small text-secondary">Output</label>
            <select id="hash-format" class="form-select">
                <option value="hex" selected>hex (lower case)</option>
                <option value="HEX">HEX (upper case)</option>
                <option value="base64">Base64</option>
            </select>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="hash-results" class="mt-4 d-flex flex-column gap-2" aria-live="polite"></div>
    {# Cloned into each result's copy button. #}
    <span id="copy-icon" hidden>{{ icons.icon("copy") }}</span>

    <div class="mt-4">
        <label for="hash-compare" class="small text-secondary">Compare with a published checksum (optional)</label>
        <input id="hash-compare" class="form-control font-monospace" type="text" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off"
            placeholder="Paste the expected hash to see if it matches">
        <p id="hash-compare-result" class="small mt-2 mb-0" role="status"></p>
    </div>
</section>
{% set variants_heading = "By algorithm" %}
{% include "tool_variants" %}
{% endblock %}

{% block about %}
<h2 class="h4">What is a hash?</h2>
<p>A hash function turns any amount of data into a short, fixed-size fingerprint. The same input always gives the
    same hash, the smallest change gives a completely different one, and you can't work back from a hash to the
    data. That makes hashes useful for checking that a file arrived intact, spotting duplicates, and storing
    fingerprints of data without the data itself.</p>

<h2 class="h4">Checking a download</h2>
<p>Many downloads publish a SHA-256 checksum next to the file. Choose the downloaded file here, paste the
    published checksum into "Compare", and you'll see whether they match. The file is read in your browser,
    a piece at a time, so even very large files work and nothing is uploaded.</p>

<h2 class="h4">Which algorithm?</h2>
<p><strong>SHA-256</strong> is the usual choice today, with SHA-512 and the SHA-3 family as strong alternatives.
    <strong>BLAKE3</strong> is a modern, very fast design. <strong>MD5</strong> and <strong>SHA-1</strong> are
    broken for security: people can make two different inputs with the same hash. They're still fine for
    spotting accidental corruption, and still widely published, so they're here for checking checksums.</p>

<h2 class="h4">HMAC</h2>
<p>An HMAC is a hash mixed with a secret key, used to check that a message came from someone who knows the key,
    for example to verify webhook signatures. Enter the key to get HMACs instead of plain hashes. BLAKE3 has its
    own keyed mode instead, so it's left out when there's a key.</p>

<h2 class="h4">Hashes and passwords</h2>
<p>Don't store passwords as plain hashes like these: they're fast to compute, so they're fast to guess. Password
    storage needs a deliberately slow function such as Argon2, scrypt or bcrypt.</p>
{% endblock %}
